    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "48c5d912_243d7523",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T00:27:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The commit explicitly mentions \"this could be seen as a regression\". The author meant that care should be applied if backporting.\n\nSince this is removing a control point, the impact of this change is linked to the SELinux policy in use. On Android, the policy for these access vectors was added in aosp/1642199. It is unspecific and mostly duplicating the fine-grain policy Android already has for its components (see also b/285443587#comment1).\n\nBy not backporting this, we have to carry on the policy which may not apply depending on the device kernel.\n\nGreg, could you please consider the backporting of this patch, because we have reviewed the impact on the Android policy it is associated with? Thanks.",
      "parentUuid": "a4714743_9bc4ebb6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "ddab7367826ada36a0cb67360948ad402019f27a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "35430941_fdcdd2e5",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-26T06:21:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changing a user-visible thing like this (i.e. a user/kernel abi) in a released kernel series should almost never be done.  Please work with the proper people and security teams to ensure that this really is needed for this already-released kernel tree, AND to ensure that it will not break any of the existing systems out there in the wild.\n\nHow are you ensuring that this will not be considered a regression on any device currently being used?",
      "parentUuid": "48c5d912_243d7523",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "ddab7367826ada36a0cb67360948ad402019f27a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15fc09fb_b511fafc",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T03:57:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this change break loading existing SELinux policies, or does it only relax the way in which existing SELinux policies are enforced?",
      "parentUuid": "35430941_fdcdd2e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "ddab7367826ada36a0cb67360948ad402019f27a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2452995_dee85532",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T05:30:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does this change break loading existing SELinux policies, or does it only relax the way in which existing SELinux policies are enforced?\n\nIt relaxes the way in which existing SELinux policies are enforced. That is, the LSM hook still exists, but SELinux does not implement it anymore. It means that SELinux will not consult the policy anymore for an access related to lockdown and consider the access as granted.\n\nBecause we granted the \"confidentiality\" access vector to domain on Android, this change is a no-op for that access vector.\n\nAndroid has a global neverallow rule on the \"integrity\" access vector, it means OEMs were not able to grant this permission to any domain.",
      "parentUuid": "15fc09fb_b511fafc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "ddab7367826ada36a0cb67360948ad402019f27a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf1d9443_b9287f1b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-28T00:06:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it is safe for Android (including for devices that are running an older Android version), then backporting this is fine.  The reasons why that is true, as well as *why* it\u0027s important that this be backported, need to be made super clear though --- in the linked bug and/or in a note at the end of the commit message.  It shouldn\u0027t be necessary to have this long discussion thread in order to get an explanation.",
      "parentUuid": "f2452995_dee85532",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "ddab7367826ada36a0cb67360948ad402019f27a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
